module

public import Theory.SpecificGroups.J2HSMultipliers.J2DoubleCover

/-!
# J₂ and Higman–Sims multiplier calculations

The checked J₂ lower bound is supplied by its actual perfect icosian double
cover, with the kernel identified as a group and the covering transported to
the permutation carrier used by the classification. Every chosen universal
cover therefore has kernel order divisible by two. The exact J₂ calculation
is reduced to its independent kernel upper bound.

The J₂ upper bound and both bounds for HS remain separate mathematical
obligations. This module does not yet assert either exact multiplier value.
The final I.1.3(1) statements are cyclic-order-two isomorphisms for the kernels
of arbitrary universal covers, as in Aschbacher–Smith, printed p.407.
-/
